From 11745fbc62f43d3ec4bdbfba6d49735323e6bb21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 18:24:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00925/11171] [outer-loop] Gemma-4 multimodal policy baselines:
 E2B + E4B both 0/37 (survive>random, no solve)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Offline air-gapped, 5 games, 60 actions:
  E2B: 0/37 levels, 0.285s/inf, 3/5 survived to budget
  E4B: 0/37 levels, 0.428s/inf, 4/5 survived to budget
Scaling E2B->E4B improves SURVIVAL (frame-aware, avoids GAME_OVER) but not SOLVING. Diagnosis:
the bottleneck is the weak per-step agent loop (sees frame + last-6 history, outputs ONE action
with NO reasoning/scratchpad, max_new=40) + ARC-AGI-3's genuine rule-induction difficulty —
not model size in the small range. Full offline competition infra now in place (eval harness +
multimodal policy pipeline + quota-gate); all policies to date = 0 levels. Next lever = agent
DESIGN (chain-of-thought reasoning + memory + systematic exploration) and/or a bigger model
(12B GGUF / frontier-multimodal), then the verifier as the efficiency layer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
